# Commit After Agent Turn

Cursor agents, background agents, and sub-agents should commit after each user prompt or completed agent task that changes tracked repo files, before handing control back.

Use `.codex/skills/commit-after-agent-turn/SKILL.md` as the shared workflow. In short: inspect status and diff, stage only intended files, run a cheap relevant validation, scan staged content for secrets, commit with prompt/tool/timing provenance, and push when the current branch already has an upstream or active PR.

Commit messages should include a redacted prompt summary, the agent/tool name, elapsed time when available, the changed files/behavior, and validation performed.

Do not commit raw API keys, `.env` files, generated logs, caches, model weights, downloaded datasets, or unrelated user changes.
